<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/5/eng@/~cl_74> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0#clause> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/5/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/5/eng@/~cl_74> <https://schema.org/text> "The principal Act is amended by inserting after the Seventh Schedule the following schedules: “EIGHTH SCHEDULE [Subsection 60(2)] PROTECTED WILDLIFE FOR THE PURPOSES OF SUBSECTION 60(2) Interpretation of the Eighth Schedule 1. Species included in this Schedule are referred to— (a) by the name of the species; or (b) as being all of the species included in a higher taxon or designated part thereof. 2. The abbreviation “spp.” is used to denote all species of a higher taxon. 3. Other references to taxa higher than species are for the purposes of information or classification only. The common names included after the scientific names of families are for reference only. They are intended to indicate the species within the family concerned that are included in this Schedule. In most cases this is not all of the species within the family. 4. Where there is conflict between a scientific name and a local name and a common name in the use of the name of any species in this Schedule, the scientific name shall prevail. Scientific Name Local Name CLASS AVES Copsychus malabaricus Murai Batu White-rumped Shama Gracula religiosa Tiong Mas Hill Myna Zosterops palpebrosus Kelicap Kunyit Oriental White Eye NINTH SCHEDULE [Paragraph 68(2)(a)] TOTALLY PROTECTED WILDLIFE FOR THE PURPOSES OF PARAGRAPH 68(2)(a) Interpretation of the Ninth Schedule 1. Species included in this Schedule are referred to— (a) by the name of the species; or (b) as being all of the species included in a higher taxon or designated part thereof. 2. The abbreviation “spp.” is used to denote all species of a higher taxon. 3. Other references to taxa higher than species are for the purposes of information or classification only. The common names included after the scientific names of families are for reference only. They are intended to indicate the species within the family concerned that are included in this Schedule. In most cases this is not all of the species within the family. 4. Where there is conflict between a scientific name and a local name and a common name in the use of the name of any species in this Schedule, the scientific name shall prevail. Scientific Name Local Name CLASS REPTILIA Varanus rudicollis Biawak Serunai Varanus dumerilii Biawak Kudung Varanus nebulosus Biawak Puru Python brongersmai Ular Sawa Darah Tomistoma schlegelii Buaya Julung-Julung Geoclemys hamiltonii Kura-kura Kolam Hitam Indotestudo elongata Baning Lonjong Manouria impressa Baning Bukit CLASS AVES Aceros subruficollis Enggang Belantara Argusianus argus Kuang Raya Buceros bicornis Enggang Papan Buceros rhinoceros Enggang Badak Pavo muticus Merak Hijau Polyplectron inopinatum Kuang Cermin Pycnonotus zeylanicus Barau-Barau Rheinardia ocellata Kuang Raya Gunung Rhynoplax vigil Enggang Tebang Mentua TENTH SCHEDULE [Paragraph 68(2)(c)] TOTALLY PROTECTED WILDLIFE FOR THE PURPOSES OF PARAGRAPH 68(2)(c) Interpretation of the Tenth Schedule 1. Species included in this Schedule are referred to— (a) by the name of the species; or (b) as being all of the species included in a higher taxon or designated part thereof. 2. The abbreviation “spp.” is used to denote all species of a higher taxon. 3. Other references to taxa higher than species are for the purposes of information or classification only. The common names included after the scientific names of families are for reference only. They are intended to indicate the species within the family concerned that are included in this Schedule. In most cases this is not all of the species within the family. 4. Where there is conflict between a scientific name and a local name and a common name in the use of the name of any species in this Schedule, the scientific name shall prevail. Scientific Name Local Name CLASS MAMMALIA Arctictis binturong Binturong Bos gaurus Seladang Capricornis sumatraensis Kambing Gurun Catopuma temminckii Kucing Tulap Dicerorhinus sumatrensis Badak Sumatera Helarctos malayanus Beruang Matahari Manis javanica Tenggiling Neofelis nebulosa Harimau Dahan Panthera pardus Harimau Kumbang Panthera tigris Harimau Belang Pardofelis marmorata Kucing Dahan Scientific Name Local Name Prionailurus planiceps Kucing Hutan Prionodon linsang Linsang Prionodon pardicolor Linsang Berbintik Pongo abelii Orang Utan Sumatra Pongo pygmaeus Orang Utan Borneo Rhinoceros sondaicus Badak Raya ELEVENTH SCHEDULE [Subsection 122(4)] DANGEROUS WILDLIFE Interpretation of the Eleventh Schedule 1. Species included in this Schedule are referred to— (a) by the name of the species; or (b) as being all of the species included in a higher taxon or designated part thereof. 2. The abbreviation “spp.” is used to denote all species of a higher taxon. 3. Other references to taxa higher than species are for the purposes of information or classification only. The common names included after the scientific names of families are for reference only. They are intended to indicate the species within the family concerned that are included in this Schedule. In most cases this is not all of the species within the family. 4. Where there is conflict between a scientific name and a local name and a common name in the use of the name of any species in this Schedule, the scientific name shall prevail. Scientific Name Local Name CLASS MAMMALIA Sus scrofa Babi Hutan Wild Pig Macaca nemestrina Beruk Pig-tailed Macaque Macaca fascicularis Kera Long-tailed Macaque CLASS REPTILIA Ophiophagus hannah Ular Tedung Selar King Cobra ”. Savings and transitional"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2021/5/eng@> .
